## #01 — Notes and one bounded adapter

Write 06.01.md first, then evidence/build05.01/CONTRACT.md before code. Read
0415.prime-cycle completely. Build a standard-library adapter under a new
labs/prime-cycle-pass01. Proposed public operations are read and record; choose
clear exact CLI names and document them. Avoid adding a general platform or an
unnecessary abstraction layer. The next user is current Prime on this desk.

Integrate reviewed reader, custody inspector/helper, review packet, review/hold,
brief/state-projection and desk-state components where their contracts fit. Pin
and invoke/import actual dependencies explicitly. Do not require every component
to run on every call just to include it. Document the real dependency graph and
unsupported mappings. Do not copy existing custody, lifecycle or report engines.
Existing modules' no-authority flags remain true to their contracts; persistence
of Prime's explicit decision is a separate attributed fact, not a tool-made grant.

## #02 — Read real sources and prepare the review fields

One registration declares one book, a small explicit set of work pages/returns,
source basis, existing review locations, output locations and bounds. No desk-wide
crawl or discovery from all directories. Reading explicitly registered real
D:/Git/lib-build work pages must be supported; do not hard-code rejection because
they live under 00.kernel. Keep Git-source and working-file observations distinct.
Do not fetch, run payloads or infer worker availability. Preserve missing/stale,
unbound, legacy-unmapped and held records as attention rather than inventing status.

Read emits a compact useful view plus an exact review-request template binding
page/pass, return/member/receipt, relevant source hashes and expected prior state.
Prime should fill judgment/reasons/next action, not recopy all mechanical hashes or
maintain coordination arrays by hand. Freshly verified custody is not acceptance.
Snapshot or bind what the reader examined; a clock field alone is not freshness.
Show recorded next actions with author and source, never choose or dispatch one.

## #03 — Record one explicit judgment beside its work

Prime supplies outcome continue/director-input/develop/complete, findings, reasons,
source references, next bounded action and unresolved matters. Keep review
disposition, pass terminal state and whole-page goal terminal state separate and
explicit. Completion needs a source-bound goal/scope identity and evidence under
the existing grant. Accepted is not automatically complete; tests are not a goal
judgment. Do not imply authentication from actor labels or approval words.
Use the accepted report/declared-hold checks where applicable; unsupported or
contradictory completion combinations must be visible/refused, not coerced.

Persist an exact structured work-local review record and its readable projection
in a declared bounded review location. Treat one as authoritative and bind the
projection to it; do not create two independently editable decision accounts.
Read must consume those completed records and derive the changed desk view without
Prime separately editing an acceptance ledger, coordination list or live file.
Declare the path/identity contract before implementation. Do not force N7NN's
exchange filenames onto ordinary work pages or modify a seated face.

Validate page/pass/origin, source and receipt identity and expected prior state
at recording. A changed relevant source must not be cleared by refreshing hashes
silently. Same review bytes/identity replay as a no-op; different bytes conflict or
require an explicit new identity and lineage, preserving predecessors. Keep exact
Director replies, original reasons, unresolved findings and capture bytes intact.
Do not treat an already manually reviewed legacy return as a newly unreviewed fact;
mark unmapped review evidence and require explicit attributed adoption if needed.

## #04 — Completion and interrupted writes

Demonstrate a finished accepted pass whose page goal stays open, and a separately
explicit completed goal that survives the next process. A new scope/goal must not
inherit old terminal completion. A Director hold remains visible and blocks its
affected action; unrelated authorized work is not globally frozen. Development
conversation stays non-executable. No automatic next pack or greater authority.

Define the completion/commit marker for a recorded review. Inject failures before,
during and after record/projection/view writes. Preserve partial files and accurate
phase/attention; never present partial work as a finished record or silently retry.
Provide a small documented inspect/recovery procedure or a safe explicit new
attempt path with lineage. Rebuild derived views from usable source records; do
not claim an atomic transaction across stores if none exists. Prevent collisions,
linked/unsafe paths, unintended source overwrites and unbounded reads/output.
State local caller trust and same-user race limits without an OS-sandbox claim.

## #05 — Tests and real-source read-only preview

Use a new disposable book and real capture/inspection where needed. Test:
1. New return, no recorded review: awaiting review.
2. Accepted pass finished, larger work-page goal open.
3. Explicit goal completion with evidence, recovered by a new process.
4. Director-input/hold, affected versus independent actions, preserved exact reply.
5. Source, receipt, origin or prior-state changes during review.
6. Identical replay, changed-content conflict and explicit successor lineage.
7. Partial writes and interrupted recovery without false completion.
8. Missing/legacy records, unknown worker and bounded source coverage.
9. Unsafe inputs, occupied destinations, dependency pin drift and output bounds.

Exercise the complete read -> fill supplied synthetic decision -> record -> new
process read path, with command transcripts and result bindings. No real model.
Then perform a read-only preview against explicitly named published sources for
0169.desk-state-preservation-0520 and its manual Prime review. Do not write a new
review to that live page as Builder. Report exactly which facts still require
Prime input and any legacy mapping limit. Show the number of manually supplied
judgment fields; no invented time/token/productivity saving or fresh-Prime claim.

